"""The mutants of C3's own part. Each row: (name, 'op', exact anchor, replacement). The anchor must occur exactly once
in the built source and be a text of op.py (mutate.py check). One mutant per constant the signers rely on, per member
of effects_of(), per refusal of validate_plan and of the precheck, per clause of the grammar of the line, per
branch of the verdict after the container, per member of the receipt; and, for the pinned probe script, one mutant per
behaviour its tests must see.

A mutant of the script (prefix S) replaces the whole constant PROBE_SCRIPT together with PROBE_SCRIPT_SHA256 and
PROBE_SCRIPT_BYTES, recomputed here from the mutated text: the source then gives the container the mutated bytes as
its own pinned ones, and only a test that RUNS the script (tests/test_probe_script.py, tests/test_native.py) or reads
its constants (tests/test_tls_probe.py) can kill it."""
import hashlib
from pathlib import Path

MUTANTS=[]
COMBOS={}
REDUNDANT={}
def add(name,old,new):MUTANTS.append((name,'op',old,new))

OWN=(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent/'op.py').read_text()
BEGIN="PROBE_SCRIPT=r'''";START=OWN.index(BEGIN);STOP=OWN.index('\n',OWN.index('PROBE_SCRIPT_BYTES='))+1
BLOCK=OWN[START:STOP];SCRIPT=BLOCK[len(BEGIN):BLOCK.index("'''\nPROBE_SCRIPT_SHA256=")]
def script(name,old,new):
    assert SCRIPT.count(old)==1,(name,SCRIPT.count(old))
    text=SCRIPT.replace(old,new);raw=text.encode('ascii')
    add(name,BLOCK,"%s%s'''\nPROBE_SCRIPT_SHA256='%s'\nPROBE_SCRIPT_BYTES=%d\n"%(BEGIN,text,hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),len(raw)))

